<title>USA: Railtex to buy Canadian Nat'l unit.</title>
<headline>Railtex to buy Canadian Nat'l unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>RailTex Inc said Monday it has signed a letter of intent with Canadian National Railway Co to buy substantially all of the assets of one Canadian's units known as the Detroit, Toledo &amp; Ironton Railroad for $27 million.</p>
<p>The company said it expects revenue from the first year of traffic after the purchase to be about $18 million and increase to $25 million in the second year.</p>
<p>RailTex said it expects the transation to close before the end of the year.</p>
</text>
